score_margins":44.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.23436576380813712,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.8312448268560759,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00896,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ocular Therapeutix, Inc., a biopharmaceutical company, engages in the development and commercialization of therapies for retinal diseases and other eye conditions using its bioresorbable hydrogel-based formulation technology in the United States. The company markets DEXTENZA, a dexamethasone ophthalmic insert to treat post-surgical ocular inflammation and pain following ophthalmic surgery, as well as allergic conjunctivitis. It is also developing AXPAXLI, an axitinib intravitreal hydrogel that is in phase 3 clinical trials for the treatment of wet age-related macular degeneration and non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy; OTX-TIC, a travoprost intracameral hydrogel, which has completed phase 2 clinical trials for the treatment of open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension. The company has a license agreement and collaboration with AffaMed Therapeutics Limited for the development and commercialization of DEXTENZA and OTX-TIC. Ocular Therapeutix, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Bedford, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Pravin U. Dugel M.D. | Executive Chairman, President & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 325 people. Revenue per employee of $160K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 47%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $133K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Ocular Therapeutix, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.4B market cap on $52M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +40% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The company is burning through $217M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -22.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 83% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 519% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 118% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ocular Therapeutix (OCUL) Stock Looks Priced For Perfection Despite Its 202% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-ocul/ocular-therapeutix/news/ocular-therapeutix-ocul-stock-looks-priced-for-perfection-de","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576054.597,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"HC Wainwright Issues Pessimistic Outlook for OCUL Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/hc-wainwright-issues-pessimistic-outlook-for-ocul-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794491092.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Ocular Therapeutix, Inc. (NASDAQ:OCUL) Consensus Forecasts Have Become A Little Darker Since Its Latest Report","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-ocul/ocular-therapeutix/news/ocular-therapeutix-inc-nasdaqocul-consensus-forecasts-have-b","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481338.633,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Ocular Therapeutix (OCUL) reports earnings tomorrow: what to expect","s